{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e","id":808423,"title":"\u201cWitnessing the Supernatural\u201d for Hunter 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-13T20:33:45-08:00","id":808423,"title":"\u201cWitnessing the Supernatural\u201d for Hunter 2e","content":"Spun off from the third Open Development thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808167#post808167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, on the subject of Hunters rapidly losing Integrity, that's going to happen whether or not killing non-humans is a Breaking Point, because \u201cwitnessing the supernatural\u201d is also a Breaking Point, and that's kind of a Hunter's whole schtick.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808170#post808170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definately gong to have to change. Perhaps immunity to that will be part of the Hunter template.<br /> <br /> IMO if Breaking Points are that common, they loose all ability to create drama or story. It would be like making feeding a Humanity 1 sin for Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808184#post808184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. I've GMed over 40 sessions of Hunter with Integrity rules, and \u201cwitnessing the supernatural\u201d had to go. It was tiring, undramatic and mechanically unsatisfying when one of the characters dropped from Integrity 7 to 3 in four sessions merely from seeing supernatural phenomena, and others had similar results. On the other hand, one character had good Resolve+Composure along with Meditative Mind 3 from the start, and lost maybe 3 points of Integrity over 11 months.<br /> <br /> And yes, the campaign was monster-of-the-week sandbox, and so I gave bonuses to rolls from killing as the monster hunting was the point of campaign. Greatest horror was gained from fucked up decisions characters did that had nothing to do with violence and spiral of despair some characters faced, not from endlessly wondering if it was wrong to dust murderous vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808185#post808185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they kind of need to be frequent to matter. It's really pretty hard to fail Breaking Point rolls, unless they have really heavy penalties.<br /> <br /> And again, there's always The Code to get rid of inconvenient Breaking Points... At a cost. There's a good reason ordinary people avoid and even willfully ignore the supernatural in the world of Chronicles of Darkness. If you're going to confront it anyway, you're going to have to deal with the consequences. For some Hunters, that will mean developing severe PTSD as they slowly succumb to Integrity loss and Condition pileup, while for others that will mean using the Code to desensitize themselves to the trauma of the supernatural, with all of the issues that come along with desensitization.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808201#post808201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better rare Breaking Points then boring Breaking Points IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808205#post808205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will only mention idea of one of users from other topic...<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807844-hunter-2e-open-dev-follow-up-hunters-and-slashers?p=807961#post807961\">SpanishInquisition wrote:</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I completely agree with this. In fact in my own GMC / Mortal Remains Hunter the Vigil game I've replaced the question, \u201cWhat have you forgotten?\u201d with \u201cWhat can't you forget?\u201d Which served to give players a definite motivation to hunt and me ideas about what sort of monsters they want to see. For example one PC survived a Slasher attack, when the Cell encountered a Slasher it put his character in the spotlight. Hunters are human - they're just incredibly committed they can't turn back.</span></span></div>And yes, Breaking Points on witnessing supernatural should be limited - I proposed in our RPG club game that till the creation of Code character need to have BP from seeing <i>all</i> supernatural - after the Code, only most mind breaking. Then I would only point this in extreme situations - like, I don't know, someone turning on the left side from the inside or something like this ( think John's Carpeneter <i>Thing</i> here situations ).<br /> <br /> Interesting would be if Hunters should be immune on Lunacy or Sleeping Curse based on resistance to Breaking Points from witnessing supernatural. But this is probably an offtopic now...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that DaveB will shoot down any suggestion of using the Code to get around the Sleeping Curse; he's said as much in the past. Likewise, I don't think Lunacy will be sidestepped in this way. And I suspect this will expand to also include similar effects such as Disquiet and Sybaris, if and when they're revised to invoke Breaking Points. It's something that ought to be pointed out in Hunter 2e, though. But I don't want to get back into this argument <i>again</i>, so I'll keep my mouth shut about it for now. If the Hunter dev is interested in my views on the subject, she can ask and I'll point out the threads where Dave and I had our knock-down drag-out fights so she can decide for herself. <br /> <br /> But the main point of the above quotes is the question of what to do about the \u201cwitness the supernatural\u201d Breaking Points in Hunter 2e. I can see three options:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Hunters are always subject to this sort of Breaking Point, unless and until they develop immunity to specific kinds of supernatural phenomena (e.g., through the Code, or by picking up an appropriate Supernatural Merit). <br /> \u2022 Hunters are never subject to this sort of Breaking Point; it's a benefit of being a hunter on par with Risking Willpower. <br /> \u2022 Some sort of compromise between the two, such as wyrdhamster's suggestion above. <br /> <br /> If Hunter 2e divorces Hunter-style Tier from GMC-style Tier and from orgs, I could see this question being answered differently based on the Hunter-style Tier: low-tier gameplay would assume that these Breaking Points are in effect by default unless and until individually bypassed; high-tier gameplay would eliminate them entirely; and mid-Tier gameplay might offer some sort of compromise such as a modified low-their model where every \u201csupernatural witness\u201d Breaking Point that's neutralized grants a bonus to resisting the ones that aren't. <br /> <br /> That said, it would probably be cleaner to pick one and apply it across the board. The first has the advantage of minimally undercutting the horror of the setting; the third has the advantage (according to Crazy_Ivan's unofficial playtesting) of making the game <i>playable</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-13-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T20:43:13-08:00","id":808428,"title":"","content":"I pretty much approach suffering from this Breaking Point as a prerequisite to becoming a capital H Hunter and that changing that Breaking Point with the Code is when the Hunter template actually crystallizes - while there might be some Hunters who gain the template without that step, they don't really stabilize and focus their mind until they do so. This doesn't give them blanket immunity from <i>actively aggressive</i> supernatural effects like the Sleeping Curse, Lunacy, Disquiet or Sybaris but it does keep their mind from trying to repress it all away, etc.<br /> <br /> (On a related note, I believe Slashers do much the same thing with at least one Breaking Point related to murder, most often dealing with premeditated murder, but that's a whole different topic.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T20:56:11-08:00","id":808432,"title":"","content":"My houserule on the matter is that if you pick up either a supernatural merit or a minor template (or both, of course), you become immune to most Breaking Points against the supernatural. You can still experience them, if they're significant enough. However, I'd allow a way for Hunters to gain Integrity immunity to some of the most dire supernatural effects (such as Lunacy) by taking the following steps:<br /> <br /> 1) Experience the supernatural effect and suffer a Breaking Point.<br /> 2) Fail the Breaking Point and lose Integrity.<br /> 3) Buy back that dot of Integrity using Practical Experience.<br /> <br /> Once the process is completed, the Hunter is now immune to, say, Lunacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T00:05:22-08:00","id":808497,"title":"","content":"The 2e development blogs for Mage suggest there's going to be a couple of extra merits in there for sleepers that don't make them immune to the sleeping curse, but help handle breaking points etc, so some of those might be useful. <br /> <br /> However, I'd suggest that an easy way to resolve this is to create an extremely minor magical merit that's easy to obtain. Something like a magical rune that grants some benefit, which turns the character into a very minor supernatural themselves. I'm thinking of the TV show Supernatural, where the two hunter characters have magical ward tattoos that protect them against demonic possession.<br /> <br /> If older experienced hunters shared the technique with new ones, it would make hunter communities largely resistant to most supernatural amnesia, except the really aggressive ones like uses of Dominate or Mind Magic, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T02:11:33-08:00","id":808528,"title":"","content":"I think you mix here a two things in your posts - &quot;Witnessing supernatural&quot; Breaking Point and Sleeping Curse ( and it's variants, like Lunacy ). <b>Mechanical </b>problem is with &quot;Witnessing supernatural&quot; - By the Integrity rules for mortals ( from <b>Chronicles of Darkness </b>rulebook ) <i>everytime</i> you see ghosts or spirits Numina, Manifestation, vampire Kissing the victim, werewolf shapeshifitng or fae losing the Mask, someone being heal by some minor witch power ( <b><i>not</i></b> the Supernal Magic of mages, it's other thing ) or <b>any</b> <b>other supernatural</b> event the mortal see - they must roll on Integrity Breaking Point for seeing &quot;<b><i>anything</i></b> supernatural&quot;.<br /> <br /> This rule have totally sense for normal mortals in Chronicle of Darkness universe - they are victims in the horror story and what they see scares them to death - but Hunters are,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807844-hunter-2e-open-dev-follow-up-hunters-and-slashers?p=807917#post807917\"> by definition</a>, mortals that should <b><i>confront </i></b>supernatural - so they should not go a bit mental unstable from every confrontation. This discussion is not about &quot;will werewolf Lunacy or mages spells lower mine Integrity&quot;. It <b>is</b> about &quot;should every supernatural occurrences lead me to emotional instability&quot;.<br /> <br /> I can understand that Sleeping Curse will still work on Hunters - even if &quot;normal&quot; supernatural events will not flinch them. ( Even if I do not agree with this, but it's other topic to talk about. ) But general rule for Hunters - &quot;Monsters do not scare us&quot; or something - should be possible, or even, part of basic Hunter Template. Hunters <b>are not</b> mortal investigators from <b>CoD</b> rulebook ( or at least it's what I read in books and hear all along on the forum ), so they<b> should not </b>be suitable to general &quot;Witness supernatural&quot; roll - or else Hunters cannot hunt, in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T02:13:45-08:00","id":808529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e#post808423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't want to get back into this argument <i>again</i></div> </div> </div> </div> Now might be a good time for the argument actually. Unless we have a specific open dev about it later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e#post808423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the main point of the above quotes is the question of what to do about the \u201cwitness the supernatural\u201d Breaking Points in Hunter 2e. I can see three options:</div> </div> </div> </div> My solution example would be a mixture of the first and second.<br /> <br /> Hunters use the Code to overwrite Witnessing the Supernatural as a breaking point. However you start play with the Code already overwriting that Breaking Point. The idea is that the &quot;What can't you forget&quot; question you use when designing Integrity was the Breaking Point you used to create your first Code. <br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of having to protect against witnessing different kinds of supernatural things individally. I think that's likely to lead to a situation like Crazy_Ivan describes. I alaways got the impression that most Hunters are always encountering new stuff for the first time.<br /> <br /> I also prefer having few Breaking Point rolls but every single one of them being a climatic moment with meingful reprocusions for the charachter. I don't think seeing a Spirit for the first time (after having already seen Vampires and Witches) is climatic.<br /> <hr /><br /> Another thing that should be debated on this subject, is what about a Hunter's supporters?<br /> <br /> The people who watch and comment on NetworkZero videos but don't approach the supernatural themselves. The engineers designing VALKARIE's Advanced Armory. The people represented by The Uninon's Friends and Neighbours Endowment.<br /> <br /> I don't think these people should all have a Tell. It just doesn't fit thematically for half the Union's town to start developing unhealthy psychological quirks because they're succeeding.<br /> <br /> My thought is that perhaps Hunters should have their own Ghoul/Wolf-Blood/etc equivilant who don't face Breaking Points for Witnessing the Supernatural but don't get any other benefits - no Risking Willpower or Practical Experience.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T02:32:01-08:00","id":808537,"title":"","content":"Actually reading the Integrity rules again I don't see anything that suggests one can't become inured to supernatural breaking points in the same way a detective could become used to dead bodies and murderers. &quot;The character witnesses something traumatic, terrifying, or that rattles his understanding of the world.&quot; isn't going to trigger the fifth time you see a ghost. Being attacked is a bit more troublesome, but even then I think if it happens enough you should definitely stop being quite so rattled about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T02:35:29-08:00","id":808540,"title":"","content":"That's also a perfectly good solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T03:22:48-08:00","id":808552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=808537#post808537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually reading the Integrity rules again I don't see anything that suggests one can't become inured to supernatural breaking points in the same way a detective could become used to dead bodies and murderers. &quot;The character witnesses something traumatic, terrifying, or that rattles his understanding of the world.&quot; isn't going to trigger the fifth time you see a ghost. Being attacked is a bit more troublesome, but even then I think if it happens enough you should definitely stop being quite so rattled about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Problem is how to gauge <i>when</i> character has become inured on &quot;Witnessing&quot; Breaking Point - Is it on second time they see a ghost? On fifth? On tenth?</b><br /> <br /> It goes further - If character has seen ghost's Manifestation, does he is inured to seeing vampires feeding? Does werewolf shapeshifting is triggering his Breaking Points? Or maybe he will have Breaking Point on seeing possession by spirits?<br /> <br /> Each character can answer differently those questions on different circumstances - and from mine experience as player in <b>Mortal Remains</b> game - they lead to unnecessary discussions each time the PCs see something spooky - not scaring, not frightening - just <i>odd</i>. It prolongs game needlessly and make ST and players to quarrel if character is or not Hunter now. It <i>literally</i> happened to me and mine PC in our game.<br /> <br /> Mine advise would to be to roleplay first scene when characters is failing this &quot;Witness supernatural&quot; Breaking Point in Prelude or first chapter of the game - when she changes from normal mortal to the hunter character - and have the all adaptations to her ( adding Code, &quot;immunity&quot; to supernatural scaring, Risking Willpower ) to be implications of this change in her Integrity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It would also by the moment when mortal changes one of Five Questions from &quot;What have you forgotten?&quot; in to &quot;What cannot you forget?&quot; - think on the scene like Sam Winchesters finding his fiancee burning on the ceiling in pilot episode of <b>Supernatural</b> series. This event will be with him for all his life and marked his path as hunter.<br /> <br /> Basically, character becomes Hunter when she goes ones for this traumatic experience of &quot;Witnessing Supernatural&quot; and as effect - instead of fear - she comes obsessed with supernatural - and changes Integrity for the Code ( even if she does not change trait name ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Thou I <i>would</i> change Hunters trait name just to Code to stress the subtle differences between it and normal humans Integrity if I made 2ED rules. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-14-2016, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T03:42:48-08:00","id":808557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=808540#post808540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's also a perfectly good solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, it does lack the &quot;murder never changes&quot; sidebar...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T04:01:19-08:00","id":808564,"title":"","content":"I personally house-rule a third Anchor to Hunters called Fixation.<br /> <br /> Mortals aren't ignorant of the supernatural so much as they aggressively deny it. That's why viewing the supernatural is a breaking point, the sight of it traumatizes them because their mind desperately wants to lock it away. In that world lies only madness and despair, but just shut your eyes and you can live a care-free life (or at least, relatively care-free that is). It's escapism done as a defensive mechanism, and when that defensive mechanism fails...<br /> <br /> Hunters are fundamentally different to mortals in that they simply can't look away. Due to a personal tragedy or some other harrowing experience, they can't deny the existence of the supernatural. They become obsessed with ridding the world of it, or at least the things that break people in body and/or mind. It's always on their mind, a Fixation. A Hunter's Fixation is what drives their hunt. It's how they personally define the Vigil for themselves. Whenever the sight of things they were not meant to see stretches their psyche to the breaking point, the Fixation is what keeps it from snapping. A Fixation could be a loved one they wish to protect, a moral principle they uphold, or a kind of monster they have vowed to rid the world of. Whatever the case, the Fixation must relate to the Vigil in some way.<br /> <br /> In game terms, a Fixation is a hybrid of a Virtue and a Trigger Point. It's like a Virtue in that if the Hunter sticks to it against difficulty (they manage to protect their loved one, uphold their principle, kill the type of monster) they regain all spent Willpower. They may do this once per chapter (thus giving them a third refill per chapter, instead of the usual two). It's like a Trigger Point in that it replaces a breaking point. If the Hunter fails to stick to their Fixation (the loved is seriously harmed or possibly killed, they go against their principle, fail to kill a monster and let it escape) they suffer a breaking point at an automatic chance die. Their psyche comes crashing down as the Vigil betrays them. Another benefit to the Fixation is that they can risk Willpower a second time in any given scene, so long as it relates to their Fixation.<br /> <br /> So basically, Fixation is the context of which the Hunter interacts with the story. It encourages both the player to defend their character's charge, as their world comes crashing down if they don't. It also gives them quite a boost to do so, as successfully defending it regains all spent Willpower, thus encouraging the player to go for broke since if they succeed they get all their Willpower back anyways. They can also risk an additional Willpower on top just for that charge, so it's quite likely they'll have two instances of risking Willpower to defend their charge, further encouraging the go-for-broke attitude. It also fits brilliantly with the all-or-nothing theme of Hunter.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Fixation does nothing to protect against things like Lunacy or Dissonance. Fixation is simply something that keeps the Hunter from ignoring the supernatural, it does nothing to protect them from active forces screwing with their head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T04:38:19-08:00","id":808579,"title":"","content":"I agree with Elfive: there comes a point when even the most outre supernatural phenomenon becomes, if not normal, at least not shocking or rattling. I think this is where the breaking-points questions need to come in - does the player feel this would be a Breaking Point for their character based on how long they've had the Vigil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:15:59-08:00","id":808665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=808537#post808537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually reading the Integrity rules again I don't see anything that suggests one can't become inured to supernatural breaking points in the same way a detective could become used to dead bodies and murderers. &amp;quot;The character witnesses something traumatic, terrifying, or that rattles his understanding of the world.&amp;quot; isn't going to trigger the fifth time you see a ghost. Being attacked is a bit more troublesome, but even then I think if it happens enough you should definitely stop being quite so rattled about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Even with base mortal characters I don't call for Breaking Point rolls every single time they see something spooky, only when it's something outside their frame of reference. And for Hunters, a lot more supernatural things are naturally going to fit within their frame of reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:11:38-08:00","id":808802,"title":"","content":"The memory loss from Quiescence is independent of the Breaking Point for witnessing the Supernal or Abyss. Whether you pass, fail, or use an ability to not have to roll it, a Hunter who isn't in the *very broad* group of Sleepwalkers will <u>still</u> forget what happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:55:11-08:00","id":808844,"title":"","content":"I don't think memory of the events is quite under the purview of the topic this thread is discussing, since it's unrelated to the Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:56:06-08:00","id":808845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=808802#post808802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The memory loss from Quiescence is independent of the Breaking Point for witnessing the Supernal or Abyss. Whether you pass, fail, or use an ability to not have to roll it, a Hunter who isn't in the *very broad* group of Sleepwalkers will <u>still</u> forget what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I would be interested in seeing how an Hunter interacts with that fact in stand of simply ignoring it as it may be felt like from Witchfinders, for it may shape mage hunting into a very interesting form other than &quot;burn the witch&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:31:09-08:00","id":808948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=808528#post808528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This rule have totally sense for normal mortals in Chronicle of Darkness universe - they are victims in the horror story and what they see scares them to death - but Hunters are,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807844-hunter-2e-open-dev-follow-up-hunters-and-slashers?p=807917#post807917\"> by definition</a>, mortals that should <b><i>confront </i></b>supernatural - so they should not go a bit mental unstable from every confrontation. This discussion is not about &quot;will werewolf Lunacy or mages spells lower mine Integrity&quot;. It <b>is</b> about &quot;should every supernatural occurrences lead me to emotional instability&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think anyone who has run Hunter with the CofD rule set has had to come up with some kind of a homebrew solution to this problem. My personal solution was to swap out Integrity for something I called Conviction.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Conviction</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Morality system described in the God Machine Chronicle replicates the degradation most mortals experience at witnessing the terrible truths of the Chronicles of Darkness. Hunters however have chosen to abandon their notions of the world in light of what they have experienced first hand and found a means of coming to term with it. Whether a single mother who takes up the Vigil after witnessing the theft of her son or a priest letting his own blood for the first time having accepted the hidden teachings of the Knights of Saint George both hunters have seen the world illuminated for what it is.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Conviction is how hunters cope with the Chronicles of Darkness, it represents the strength of commitment to the Vigil as well as their own ability to withstand the horror of what they have chosen to stand against. As such it is as much a product of the hunters own belief as well as their overall mental well being. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">While Conviction is slightly more robust, at least in terms of how the <i>supernatural </i> effects a character's psychological well being (again hunters have made a conscious decision to hold a light to the darkness) the murder of a human being is always a breaking point at least until a hunter redefines his definition of human.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The following questions help to define the character's breaking points and their relationship to the Vigil.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>What is the worst thing your character can imagine himself doing in pursuit of the Vigil? </i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In choosing to confront the inhuman how inhumane is a character prepared to act? What is the line that your character would not cross? What is he prepared to do to save himself or another? Would he torture a monster's servant or use an innocent as bait?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>What is the worst thing your character can imagine someone else doing?</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Monsters (human or otherwise) are capable of atrocities that can destroy minds and rend souls. What is the worst thing your character can imagine befalling someone (or himself)? Is it the thought of a monster destroying his family? The possession of an innocent? Cannibalism?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>What can't your character forget?</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A character who carries the Vigil their first exposure to the supernatural often leaves them with memories they cannot let go of. Decide what memories the character carries with them. Did she lose her father to living shadows? Watch helplessly as her mentor was burned alive by a spirit? Kill someone under a vampire's command? Describe this event in as much detail as you can. This is a breaking point in its own right and sets a benchmark for what your character would have to be exposed to experience one now.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>What does your character believe?</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This is a belief that the character holds most deeply, the center by which a hunter holds himself in the face of experiences that threaten to overwhelm him. Note that this is something the character clings to without rational proof. Is it faith in a higher power or some conspiracy theory? Intrinsic loyalty of family? Scientific rationalism? Fate or some greater destiny?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Who or what is the enemy?</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What is a monster? Where is the line between human and inhuman? Is it biological? The existence of a soul? The definition of a behavior? Or is anything with abnormal &quot;power&quot; a potential target? This establishes not just a single breaking point but helps define what the character defines as murder.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> I also had each Tell be a persistent Condition you gained by choosing to change the answer to one of the questions above, rather than roll for a breaking point. <br /> <br /> I think the point here is that there needs to be some alternation to how Hunters confront with the supernatural - not the blanket kind of immunity that say becoming one of HtR's Imbued (cannot become a monster, spend a point to become immune to mind control, etc.) offered - but some system that makes them capable of engaging in a protracted conflict with the supernatural as well as rules to tweak that to your liking. So if you want to play 'Blade' then you can, but if you're looking for 'Frailty' you've got other options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:55:35-08:00","id":809056,"title":"","content":"I think my preferred answer to this is something akin to what SpahishInquisition describes. Hunters shouldn't be able to completely ignore the instinctual gut reaction CofD mortals have to the supernatural. But they should be able to interact with it differently, so they can engage in prolonged conflict with it - whether it's an old-school stakes-and-shotguns hunt, research, rescue attempt or negotiations.<br /> <br /> The more actively mind-screwy effects, such as the Quiessence Curse or Lunacy, are something different. But hunters do need some way to overcome them. It shouldn't be <i>easy</i>, and should probably mess with their heads in a different way, but it should be possible.<br /> <br /> As I've said before, this is a bigger thing than just crossing Hunter over with other gamelines. Hunter is unlike any other gameline, since hunters are still mortals. Their capabilities have a much more pervasive impact on the general dynamics of the World of Darkness, should one choose to include them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:30:12-08:00","id":809242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=808529#post808529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that should be debated on this subject, is what about a Hunter's supporters?<br /> <br /> The people who watch and comment on NetworkZero videos but don't approach the supernatural themselves. The engineers designing VALKARIE's Advanced Armory. The people represented by The Uninon's Friends and Neighbours Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think watching footage of the supernatural would depend on whether or not you believed it was real. TFV's engineers would depend on whether they knew what the weapons were being used for; if you actually SEE that new kind of bullets you made tested on a &quot;live&quot; vampire, that might unnerve you. Friends and Neighbors would really depend, once again, on specifics.<br /> <br /> My two cents on the whole topic is that it's largely subjective; a newbie hunter sees a ghost, they get scared. A veteran sees a Centimanus' using the more extreme Pandoran Transmutation's might not even blink. I think it also depends on the individual; an arachnophobe, no matter how experienced, freaks out when they see a man disintegrate into a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qTNZOjPhQao\" target=\"_blank\">pile of spiders</a>.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">(I know those are ants, I couldn't find a clip with spiders<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 01-15-2016, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:46:02-08:00","id":809258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=808537#post808537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually reading the Integrity rules again I don't see anything that suggests one can't become inured to supernatural breaking points in the same way a detective could become used to dead bodies and murderers. &amp;quot;The character witnesses something traumatic, terrifying, or that rattles his understanding of the world.&amp;quot; isn't going to trigger the fifth time you see a ghost. Being attacked is a bit more troublesome, but even then I think if it happens enough you should definitely stop being quite so rattled about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that even if this is not the way said rule was intended to be interpreted where blue-book mortals are concerned, it makes perfect sense as the interpretation to be used in the context of <b>Hunter</b>. That is, I'd like to see <b>Hunter</b> go with this <i>even if</i> we end up getting further clarification to the effect that regular mortals never get to the point where a given supernatural phenomenon doesn't bother them anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T19:26:35-08:00","id":809299,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth looking in the Chronicles of Darkness book again and looking at the section on Integrity. Don't have access right now, but I do feel the language on the &quot;what have you forgotten?&quot; Question might be worth looking at again vis a vis supernatural breaking points.<br /> <br /> I also don't think it's appropriate for Hunters to avoid the breaking point for seeing the supernatural. I definitely think they should be more effective in resisting if, possibly through dice bonuses and a different set of Conditions for success, but the risk that you'll lose your nerve, that it'll wear you down, that it can BREAK you should always be present. It's an important part of the drama of Hunter.<br /> <br /> To draw one comparison, in XCOM it's not that your higher level troopers CANT become panicked, it's that they're less likely to. The risk is always there and oh nelly, it's bad when it happens.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, so looking at the text:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness Corebook, pg. 30</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What has your character forgotten? In the Chronicles of<br /> Darkness, it\u2019s next to impossible to grow up without<br /> any exposure to the supernatural. Decide what your<br /> character saw and forgot. Did she see a vampire take<br /> the form of smoke and vanish? A man turn into a<br /> wolf? Maybe she caught a glimpse of an impossible<br /> nightmarescape through a door that should never<br /> have been propped open? Describe this scene in as<br /> much detail as you can. <b>This is a breaking point that<br /> already occurred, but it helps set a benchmark for<br /> what your character would have to see in order to<br /> experience one now.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. This implies something something interesting for the conversation, doesn't it? That this thing seen before helps determine on a case by case basis what might constitute a breaking point versus what doesn't when it's supernatural and you see it? I don't know if that solves the problem but it strikes me as interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 01-14-2016, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T20:56:47-08:00","id":809351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=809299#post809299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's worth looking in the Chronicles of Darkness book again and looking at the section on Integrity. Don't have access right now, but I do feel the language on the &amp;quot;what have you forgotten?&amp;quot; Question might be worth looking at again vis a vis supernatural breaking points..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea. Looks like we've got:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What has your character forgotten? In the Chronicles of Darkness, it\u2019s next to impossible to grow up without any exposure to the supernatural. Decide what your character saw and forgot. Did she see a vampire take the form of smoke and vanish? A man turn into a wolf? Maybe she caught a glimpse of an impossible nightmarescape through a door that should never have been propped open? Describe this scene in as much detail as you can. This is a breaking point that already occurred, but <b>it helps set a benchmark for what your character would have to see in order to experience one now.</b> </div> </div> </div>Bolded for emphasis. I think we have our answer right here. Witnessing the supernatural <i>can</i> be a Breaking Point, but the bar is set by past experience. I would personally apply that same guideline to Hunters. If they've been around the block a few times, they're not going to experience Breaking Points for a lot of stuff normal people might. But really weird shit might still be a Break, at least at first. But after a while they'll get accustomed to that too, and that sets a new baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:07:44-08:00","id":809678,"title":"","content":"I do think its worth mentioning that the Integrity Degeneration doesn't exist in quite as much a vacuum as morality degeneration did. You can actually build a character who, while no suffering checks no less frequently than a normal human, are considerably less likely to suffer any long term consequences of it. (You're still probably going to pick up a condition, but Shaken and Spooked are pretty much just &quot;here's temporary way to get another beat&quot; anyway.)<br /> <br /> The Hunter template could provide free points to resolve/composure, or provide some Vigil-Context specific merits that provide additional boosts to resolve+composure checks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T10:40:15-08:00","id":810681,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of adding &quot;what can't you forget&quot; as a Hunter specific Integrity question. And I can't decide which of the supernatural breaking point ideas I prefer. I do love the idea of the expanding experiences mean fewer breaking points for truly weird stuff. But I also love the idea that a Hunter &quot;starts&quot; with a Code trade-off to remove it. The former supports the Horror angle, especially for fresh-new-hunter games. But the latter sets Hunter apart from baseline mortal right away, with a Hunter having to adopt a Code right off the bat just to hunt effectively. As for the known crossover effects, most of them only come up if the ST is using the game's corebook rather than the Hunter core. IIRC, all of them but Disquiet have a merit to avoid it (sleepwalker, witness, breaking-point-based wolfblood, stigmatic, etc). Granted, most of those start to blur the human template... but hey, thats a feature, not a bug, especially for tier 1 and 2 hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T11:04:51-08:00","id":810694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/808423-\u201cwitnessing-the-supernatural\u201d-for-hunter-2e?p=810681#post810681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea of adding &quot;what can't you forget&quot; as a Hunter specific Integrity question. And I can't decide which of the supernatural breaking point ideas I prefer. I do love the idea of the expanding experiences mean fewer breaking points for truly weird stuff. But I also love the idea that a Hunter &quot;starts&quot; with a Code trade-off to remove it. The former supports the Horror angle, especially for fresh-new-hunter games. But the latter sets Hunter apart from baseline mortal right away, with a Hunter having to adopt a Code right off the bat just to hunt effectively. As for the known crossover effects, most of them only come up if the ST is using the game's corebook rather than the Hunter core. IIRC, all of them but Disquiet have a merit to avoid it (sleepwalker, witness, breaking-point-based wolfblood, stigmatic, etc). Granted, most of those start to blur the human template... but hey, thats a feature, not a bug, especially for tier 1 and 2 hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The great thing is, they don't have to be mutually exclusive. With what counts as a Breaking Point being determined by past experience, each player can decide where their character lies on the spectrum from &quot;I roll Breaking Points for seeing my own shadow&quot; to &quot;I laugh in Chthuhlu's face&quot; based on their character background and their answers to the five questions. If you want to play a game where Hunters start out immune to Breaking Points from witnessing the supernatural, just generate characters who have seen some shit (even if they have little practical experience, they might still have witnessed horrific things) and don't roll Breaking Points for witnessing the supernatural. If you want to play a game where any supernatural event is a potential Breaking Point, have all of the characters generate normal mortal characters and add the Hunter template during play. If you want a mix of the two, have each player decide individually how much experience they've had with the supernatural and work out what kinds of things might count as Breaking Points for them to witness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T09:35:21-08:00","id":811167,"title":"","content":"Speaking of them not being mutually exclusive. Some Hunters might use The Code to essentially skip to the end, essentially using a breaking point from seeing a boring old Ghoul to create a Code and immunise themselves to seeing Kerberoi and other really freaky stuff.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you play it this could be kinda a bad idea - in that long after you've seen too much stuff you're still stuck with the code and it's Tell or whatever drawbacks 2E has. Or it could be a very practical choice, because if you've seen Vampires, Sin-Eaters, Demons going loud; then the one time you <b>REALLY</b> don't want to have a Breaking Point is when you're face to face with something that's so much freakier that you still find it shocking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-18-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}